Psa 78:1 , An exhortation both to learn and to preach, the law of God;
Psa 78:9 , The story of God's wrath against the incredulous and disobedient;
Psa 78:67 , The Israelites being rejected, God chose Judah, Zion, and David.
Asaph, to give instruction.
Psa 74:1 *title This Psalm was probably written, as Calmet and others suppose, by Asaph in the days of Asa, who had gained, by the aid of the Syrians, a great victory over the Israelites, and brought back to the pure worship of God many out of the tribes of Ephraim, Manasseh, and Simeon. 2Chr. 15:1-16:14
